# Docker build context is backend/ when building identity service.
# Reduces context size and avoids sending secrets into the daemon.

# Dependencies — reinstalled in container
**/node_modules

# Build output — rebuilt in container
**/dist

# Tests and dev tooling — not needed in production image
**/tests
**/*.test.ts
**/*.spec.ts
**/vitest.config.ts
**/__tests__
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example

# Editor and OS
**/.DS_Store
**/.idea
**/.vscode
**/Thumbs.db

# Version control
**/.git
**/.gitignore

# Docker
**/Dockerfile*
**/.dockerignore

# Other services — only identity and shared-utils are needed for identity image
# (Uncomment to shrink context further; then copy only identity + shared-utils in Dockerfile)
# services/core-platform
# services/communications
# services/payments-penalties
# services/allocation
